Z||000000||BroCar 87||04-28-2000||06:22 PM||||Its on my 4 cyl.     Well I was putting the wrench on the old O2 sensor and barely put any pressure on it and SNAP it broke off. There is now a quarter size hole in my manifold facing my seats BOOOOOO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I need to do something, my whole exhaust is in bad shape. In the meantime, Is there a way to "rig" this until I can get my new manifold in? Also where is the best place to get a manifold? I will do the rest of the exhaust later. I NEED the manifold. <BR>Any help on this would be appreciated||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||04-29-2000||05:06 AM||||Hey Bro, I did the same damn thing when I had my 2M4 5 years ago! My dumb ass tried to JB weld the thing back on <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Well, it was high heat JB weld <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It lasted a whole 2 minutes and cooked off! I got a new manifold from the Fiero Store but looking back I'm thinking would have made more sense to save cash to take the manifold off and having the doohickey welded back on again?||||reg||2
Z||000002||theogre||04-29-2000||02:15 PM||||these manifolds area available off other GM cars. go visit the local scrap yard.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-29-2000||04:16 PM||||I agree with Ogre. Going through the salvage yard I couldn't beleive how many manifolds were ready to be taken. AND they are in the front face of the engine! What could be easier! Take it throw it away and grab another. Its rare to actually have a Fiero part in such plentiful supply!||||reg||14
